WEBVTT

00:09.009 --> 00:10.218
[tense music playing]

00:12.429 --> 00:13.471
[both grunt]

00:14.097 --> 00:15.223
[grunting]

00:16.057 --> 00:16.933
Go!

00:22.814 --> 00:23.773
Whoa!

00:27.944 --> 00:28.778
[grunts]

00:31.823 --> 00:32.782
[grunts]

00:34.617 --> 00:35.869
[both panting]

00:39.414 --> 00:40.498
[grunts]

00:41.624 --> 00:42.917
[music intensifies]

00:44.544 --> 00:46.755
- [gasps]
- Stop!

00:46.838 --> 00:48.214
[panting]

00:51.092 --> 00:52.010
Damn it!

00:52.594 --> 00:53.428
Drop the bag!

00:53.511 --> 00:55.513
[whimpering] Oh, shit!

00:56.765 --> 00:58.516
- [goon] Come here!
- [Woo-jin panting]

00:58.600 --> 00:59.601
[grunts]

00:59.684 --> 01:00.852
Start the car!

01:02.937 --> 01:04.647
Hurry up! Hurry. Run faster.

01:08.443 --> 01:10.195
Hurry, hurry! Come on!

01:11.654 --> 01:13.198
Start the car!

01:15.075 --> 01:17.202
- Bastards.
- [Woo-jin] Run faster!

01:17.285 --> 01:18.536
- Hurry!
- [Hyeon-ju grunts]

01:20.163 --> 01:21.498
[Gun-woo] Please hurry up.

01:21.581 --> 01:24.793
Come on. Door. Door. Door.
Come on, let's go!

01:24.876 --> 01:26.127
[tires screeching]

01:29.589 --> 01:31.257
[all panting]

01:35.637 --> 01:37.263
God dammit.

01:37.347 --> 01:39.349
[theme music playing]

02:00.745 --> 02:04.249
BLOODHOUNDS

02:05.083 --> 02:08.837
People borrowing from Kim Myeong-gil
is way more than we thought.

02:09.337 --> 02:12.340
They all enter the bar
in one-hour intervals.

02:13.174 --> 02:15.426
Some of them in official police vehicles.

02:15.927 --> 02:16.803
[inhales sharply]

02:16.886 --> 02:18.388
I don't know his name,

02:18.972 --> 02:21.474
but there was also
a professional baseball player.

02:21.558 --> 02:22.684
[inhales deeply]

02:23.226 --> 02:24.435
[sighs deeply]

02:24.519 --> 02:27.105
Yeah, well, seems he's expanded his reach.

02:27.605 --> 02:28.439
[inhales deeply]

02:35.238 --> 02:37.240
[coughing]

02:38.741 --> 02:39.576
[coughs]

02:40.660 --> 02:41.494
[coughs]

02:43.454 --> 02:44.372
[Mr. Choi coughs]

02:45.832 --> 02:48.960
I knew it
that Myeong-gil was an ex-convict.

02:50.086 --> 02:51.504
He begged for my help.

02:51.588 --> 02:53.756
He said all he wanted was a fresh start.

02:53.840 --> 02:54.716
[inhales sharply]

02:55.300 --> 02:56.759
And like an idiot…

02:59.137 --> 03:00.930
[sighs] I fell for it.

03:03.183 --> 03:05.143
After Myeong-gil screwed me,

03:06.436 --> 03:08.521
I went into hiding with Mr. Oh.

03:09.480 --> 03:12.192
That's when I heard rumors
that he'd started a company

03:12.859 --> 03:15.236
using the money and bonds
he had stolen from me.

03:17.197 --> 03:19.782
I should've taken care of him
a long time ago.

03:20.867 --> 03:22.785
I taught him everything.

03:22.869 --> 03:24.245
[inhales deeply]

03:25.163 --> 03:26.331
[exhales deeply]

03:27.916 --> 03:29.250
I didn't have the courage.

03:31.127 --> 03:33.171
I wish I would've gained some by now.

03:35.757 --> 03:37.634
I shouldn't have stopped you
from going after him

03:37.717 --> 03:39.344
and giving him what he deserved.

03:40.428 --> 03:41.304
I'm sorry.

03:42.847 --> 03:45.558
I was too afraid I'd lose you as well.

03:52.774 --> 03:53.816
You've always…

03:55.818 --> 03:58.321
cared for me and protected me
like I was family.

04:00.531 --> 04:02.158
I'm always… [inhales sharply]

04:02.909 --> 04:06.120
…ready to lay my life on the line for you
anytime you need it, sir.

04:07.580 --> 04:08.414
I know you are.

04:10.708 --> 04:11.542
And I'm sorry.

04:14.420 --> 04:15.797
[cell phone vibrating]

04:20.843 --> 04:21.678
Hello.

04:23.429 --> 04:25.223
Okay. [sighs]

04:26.724 --> 04:27.684
Come on back.

04:31.729 --> 04:35.024
So, uh, it seems the kids just got jumped

04:35.942 --> 04:37.527
while they were moving all the money.

04:38.194 --> 04:40.571
- Are they hurt?
- No, they didn't mention it.

04:41.072 --> 04:42.073
But, uh,

04:43.658 --> 04:45.576
they said they lost the money
from the safe.

04:45.660 --> 04:47.287
Are they hurt or not?

04:48.121 --> 04:49.622
I think they're all right.

04:50.540 --> 04:51.457
[exhales deeply]

04:52.792 --> 04:57.463
They also… tied one of them up
but didn't want to finish him off.

04:57.547 --> 04:58.506
Now what?

05:00.466 --> 05:03.761
When an ER receives a patient
that was injured doing something illegal…

05:03.845 --> 05:04.804
[inhales sharply]

05:04.887 --> 05:07.223
…the doctors are obligated
to call the police.

05:07.849 --> 05:10.685
That's why
I used to have surgeons of my own

05:10.768 --> 05:12.353
ready to operate at all times.

05:13.813 --> 05:16.399
I'm pretty sure Myeong-gil must have
a similar arrangement.

05:17.317 --> 05:19.652
I'll go get Du-yeong.
He's gonna find him fast.

05:19.736 --> 05:22.572
- [dramatic music playing]
- [In-beom heavy, rapid breathing]

05:23.156 --> 05:24.991
- [bones crack]
- [shouts, groans]

05:31.039 --> 05:32.665
[yelling]

05:33.291 --> 05:34.751
[In-beom grunting]

05:40.673 --> 05:41.924
[coughing]

05:47.263 --> 05:48.389
[In-beom coughing]

05:51.642 --> 05:53.561
[suspenseful music playing]

06:11.662 --> 06:12.622
Good job.

06:14.123 --> 06:14.999
Hey.

06:18.753 --> 06:19.837
Good job.

06:20.546 --> 06:21.631
Uh, yeah.

06:22.715 --> 06:26.219
Get some sleep, okay?
Come to the restaurant tomorrow.

06:27.428 --> 06:29.389
[hesitating] What? Uh, what for?

06:30.348 --> 06:31.182
For food.

06:32.642 --> 06:33.476
Oh.

06:35.436 --> 06:36.437
Okay?

06:37.855 --> 06:39.399
I don't usually eat lunch.

06:39.482 --> 06:40.942
- You will.
- Yeah.

06:42.360 --> 06:43.319
Go on.

06:47.490 --> 06:48.366
[Hyeon-ju grunts]

06:51.077 --> 06:52.537
- [Gun-woo exhales]
- Hey.

06:52.620 --> 06:54.372
[Mr. Choi grunting]

06:57.750 --> 06:58.793
You okay?

07:01.170 --> 07:03.840
We lost all the money
in the safe. I'm really sorry.

07:03.923 --> 07:05.800
But you're not hurt anywhere, right?

07:06.467 --> 07:07.301
Oh.

07:08.428 --> 07:09.262
No.

07:10.596 --> 07:11.806
That's all that matters.

07:11.889 --> 07:13.141
[gentle piano music playing]

07:13.224 --> 07:17.270
Oh. I… I have more boxes to move.
You should sleep.

07:22.024 --> 07:24.026
Hyeon-ju, are you sure you're not hurt?

07:28.030 --> 07:28.865
Yeah.

07:41.878 --> 07:43.254
[shallow breathing]

08:00.980 --> 08:02.565
[In-beom grunting]

08:15.244 --> 08:17.580
[engine revving]

08:19.040 --> 08:21.042
[dramatic music playing]

08:23.294 --> 08:25.880
It's not that I didn't pay them back,
but this guy just came in…

08:27.548 --> 08:29.592
[Jang-do] In-beom is going to be fine,

08:30.176 --> 08:31.511
but his eardrum is busted.

08:33.137 --> 08:35.723
I got a license plate.
I'll run it through tomorrow.

08:36.682 --> 08:37.975
What do you mean "tomorrow"?

08:39.101 --> 08:41.604
That's when
the officers we pay are on duty.

08:41.687 --> 08:42.647
[chuckles]

08:44.232 --> 08:45.608
Watch your tone with me.

08:48.069 --> 08:49.111
Don't push me.

08:49.779 --> 08:50.905
Ah, shit. [clicks tongue]

08:53.658 --> 08:54.492
[lighter clicks]

08:56.160 --> 08:56.994
[Jang-do sighs]

08:58.162 --> 09:01.457
If it's an unregistered vehicle
or fake plates,

09:01.541 --> 09:04.794
is it possible to track it
with the security cameras?

09:06.295 --> 09:08.798
It's definitely possible,
but it would take us a little while.

09:09.465 --> 09:12.260
License plates can be looked up
on the police Intranet.

09:12.843 --> 09:14.845
But if we're talking about
getting security footage,

09:14.929 --> 09:18.808
that's a different story. We'd have to…
be able to get inside control centers,

09:18.891 --> 09:20.977
and I would need to pay off
the right kinds of people.

09:21.769 --> 09:23.020
Money is not an issue.

09:23.563 --> 09:24.939
Just get it done quickly.

09:25.773 --> 09:26.607
Yes.

09:26.691 --> 09:29.193
I want you to find out
who owns the building.

09:29.944 --> 09:32.655
If it's Choi,
you need to get his home address.

09:33.531 --> 09:34.365
Yeah.

09:34.448 --> 09:35.533
You can go now.

09:36.200 --> 09:37.618
Let me talk to Jang-do.

09:39.203 --> 09:40.037
Sir?

09:42.373 --> 09:43.457
You heard me.

09:47.336 --> 09:48.421
Sure.

09:54.677 --> 09:55.553
[lighter clicks]

10:01.892 --> 10:02.727
[lighter clicks]

10:09.442 --> 10:10.276
Beom,

10:11.235 --> 10:12.737
why do you think they left him there?

10:14.530 --> 10:16.282
Is it because they had run out of time?

10:16.991 --> 10:19.160
Jang-do. Jang-do, huh?

10:20.077 --> 10:22.496
You're thinking far too positively
right now.

10:23.664 --> 10:25.458
Think negatively for a change.

10:26.125 --> 10:27.585
Try to understand.

10:27.668 --> 10:29.170
Those bastards are trying to kill you.

10:29.253 --> 10:32.048
You should allow that idea
to drive your thoughts.

10:32.131 --> 10:33.549
So why'd they leave him there?

10:36.385 --> 10:38.387
- They're planning to track him.
- [scoffs]

10:40.723 --> 10:42.016
Okay then.

10:42.099 --> 10:44.769
We need to get more men
and put them at the hospital.

10:45.603 --> 10:46.437
Yes.

10:48.356 --> 10:49.857
And we need to follow Jun-min.

10:52.777 --> 10:54.028
Why? Did he do something wrong?

10:54.111 --> 10:57.281
Uh, I told you to think negatively
about this.

10:58.449 --> 11:00.785
Mr. Choi may have info on him.

11:02.620 --> 11:03.663
Ah.

11:04.580 --> 11:07.208
[inhales sharply]
Jun-min is just a coward.

11:07.792 --> 11:09.502
He's turned way too easily.

11:10.169 --> 11:11.295
It'll be very obvious.

11:11.379 --> 11:13.923
One look at his face,
and he just gives everything away, huh?

11:15.257 --> 11:16.092
Sir.

11:16.175 --> 11:17.259
[inhales sharply]

11:17.927 --> 11:19.053
All right now.

11:19.762 --> 11:21.597
Beom is just a small fry here.

11:22.598 --> 11:23.891
So Lee Du-yeong is our man.

11:23.974 --> 11:25.226
He's got a bike.

11:25.309 --> 11:27.186
That's who they'll send to tail him.

11:27.269 --> 11:28.104
Yeah.

11:28.187 --> 11:30.648
Block the streets and trap him.

11:33.234 --> 11:34.068
Yes.

11:35.361 --> 11:36.821
[chuckles] Should be fun.

11:36.904 --> 11:38.072
- [clicks tongue]
- [music stops]

11:44.620 --> 11:45.454
[exhales deeply]

11:48.082 --> 11:48.916
[exhales deeply]

11:50.251 --> 11:51.168
[exhales deeply]

11:53.212 --> 11:54.714
[heavy breathing]

12:02.388 --> 12:03.222
Oh!

12:04.056 --> 12:05.099
Did you sleep well, sir?

12:05.850 --> 12:07.059
Did you get any sleep?

12:07.810 --> 12:08.644
Yeah.

12:08.728 --> 12:11.105
You got back so late. You should rest now.

12:11.188 --> 12:12.857
I got plenty of sleep, but thank you.

12:12.940 --> 12:14.024
Ah, Gun-woo,

12:14.525 --> 12:16.277
I've been meaning
to talk to you, actually.

12:16.360 --> 12:17.194
Oh.

12:20.197 --> 12:21.574
[Mr. Choi grunting]

12:22.324 --> 12:27.705
Hyeon-ju, uh… You may have noticed
she always has a bit of an edge to her.

12:27.788 --> 12:28.622
Oh.

12:29.415 --> 12:33.085
I think that's the reason why
she acts a little cold at times. [laughs]

12:33.919 --> 12:35.421
Ah. [inhales sharply]

12:36.505 --> 12:38.632
But she seems
to have softened considerably

12:38.716 --> 12:39.884
since meeting you and Woo-jin.

12:39.967 --> 12:42.470
For that, you have my gratitude.

12:43.804 --> 12:45.556
We really enjoyed working with Hyeon-ju.

12:45.639 --> 12:47.057
Oh, very good.

12:47.141 --> 12:49.143
So, the money I paid you in advance,

12:50.144 --> 12:51.020
it's gone.

12:52.104 --> 12:55.775
Oh, so… where did the money go then?

12:55.858 --> 12:58.068
I meant to say that we're even now.

12:58.152 --> 12:59.612
Oh, why?

12:59.695 --> 13:03.741
Do you have any idea
how much money you managed to recover?

13:04.408 --> 13:05.743
Uh, well…

13:05.826 --> 13:06.744
[inhales sharply]

13:08.412 --> 13:09.663
[chuckles softly]

13:10.748 --> 13:14.668
I'm going to give you a nice bonus
for a safe transport.

13:14.752 --> 13:16.170
Oh, uh… [inhales sharply]

13:17.087 --> 13:19.548
I'd like to pay it back
by putting my fair share of work, sir.

13:19.632 --> 13:21.383
You've already done your share.

13:22.510 --> 13:24.845
You three managed
to retrieve a considerable sum.

13:26.096 --> 13:27.056
[exhales deeply]

13:27.681 --> 13:31.352
So from this moment,
you're not indebted to me anymore.

13:31.936 --> 13:36.440
Get your mom
and go open a new café somewhere nice.

13:38.150 --> 13:40.152
I'll make all the necessary investments.

13:40.236 --> 13:41.487
[chuckles softly]

13:43.531 --> 13:45.866
Thank you so much, Mr. Choi.

13:46.367 --> 13:49.537
I want to help you catch Kim Myeong-gil

13:50.746 --> 13:52.081
I'll do that until the very end.

13:52.164 --> 13:53.707
You've been very helpful.

13:53.791 --> 13:56.418
I know that,
but I'd like to see it to the very end.

13:57.920 --> 13:58.754
Why?

13:59.880 --> 14:00.965
To repay my debt.

14:01.549 --> 14:03.008
You've done enough already.

14:03.092 --> 14:04.718
It's not enough in my book, sir.

14:05.886 --> 14:08.097
It's not over until it's over for real.

14:09.515 --> 14:12.434
[chuckles] Yeah.

14:14.270 --> 14:17.523
- It's not over till it's over for real.
- [exhales deeply]

14:18.107 --> 14:19.859
We should have a drink sometime soon.
[laughs]

14:20.568 --> 14:22.945
Oh, I don't really drink, unfortunately.

14:23.654 --> 14:24.530
Huh.

14:24.613 --> 14:26.532
I'll be more than happy
to pour your drinks, sir.

14:27.491 --> 14:28.868
[both laughing]

14:31.078 --> 14:32.872
- Go on.
- Oh, okay.

14:39.128 --> 14:40.504
[inhales sharply]

14:58.606 --> 15:00.900
Use wasabi and soy sauce.

15:00.983 --> 15:03.277
[breathes deeply]

15:07.281 --> 15:08.407
Mm.

15:12.536 --> 15:14.163
[light rock music playing]

15:22.004 --> 15:23.005
Wild caught.

15:24.423 --> 15:28.886
You see, farmed halibut have a lot of fat
in their fins that can be too heavy.

15:28.969 --> 15:33.474
But wild ones like this
have all that fat evenly distributed.

15:33.557 --> 15:38.354
[inhales sharply]
It's such a clean and exquisite flavor.

15:39.605 --> 15:41.190
I can still taste it.

15:41.732 --> 15:43.150
And it's aged to perfection.

15:43.734 --> 15:44.777
Huh.

15:45.444 --> 15:47.821
You? An expert?

15:47.905 --> 15:49.531
Oh… [inhales sharply]

15:49.615 --> 15:51.575
I was a restaurant YouTuber
back in the day,

15:51.659 --> 15:54.328
but my channel
didn't get enough subscribers, so I quit.

15:54.411 --> 15:57.039
This was my first time having it cut long.

15:57.790 --> 15:59.792
It wraps around your mouth like a whip.

16:00.876 --> 16:03.671
That was the best halibut
I've ever had, sir.

16:04.713 --> 16:05.547
Love it.

16:05.631 --> 16:06.757
[chuckles softly]

16:06.840 --> 16:08.258
That was amazing.

16:08.342 --> 16:10.636
Hey, I'm a hustler.

16:10.719 --> 16:11.929
I'll subscribe.

16:12.012 --> 16:13.722
- I told you it's over.
- Oh.

16:14.348 --> 16:15.766
You kids went through a lot.

16:16.642 --> 16:18.060
That's why I wanted to treat you.

16:18.143 --> 16:19.603
- Thank you, sir.
- Thank you.

16:19.687 --> 16:21.271
What do you plan to do now?

16:21.855 --> 16:23.357
Well, kill the big guy.

16:24.817 --> 16:27.027
Then catch the one
that looks like a wildcat.

16:27.611 --> 16:29.822
That one is Kim Myeong-gil's cleanup crew.

16:31.281 --> 16:35.035
He's the one they send around
buying people's silence

16:35.119 --> 16:37.621
and threatening their lives
whenever it's needed.

16:38.747 --> 16:39.665
We'll fuck him up.

16:40.541 --> 16:43.043
And then he's going to lead us
to where the bodies are buried.

16:43.127 --> 16:45.170
Then we'll have Kim Myeong-gil.

16:45.254 --> 16:47.756
- Then Smile Capital is over.
- [Yang-jung] That's right.

16:49.258 --> 16:51.635
Well, what do we do
if we don't find any bodies?

16:51.719 --> 16:55.764
Well, we can find a murder weapon
or maybe some security footage.

16:57.766 --> 16:58.600
Here.

16:59.393 --> 17:01.937
[inhales sharply] As for the yellowtail,

17:03.105 --> 17:04.231
the age--

17:04.314 --> 17:05.357
Oh, sorry I'm late.

17:06.775 --> 17:08.610
- Sit, sit. Sit, sit.
- Took your time.

17:09.111 --> 17:11.488
Lee Du-yeong.
Nice to meet you. Pound this.

17:11.572 --> 17:12.990
- Kim Gun-woo, sir.
- [Du-yeong] Uh-huh.

17:13.073 --> 17:17.494
- Hong Woo-jin.
- Oh, boxer fists. Hello.

17:18.245 --> 17:20.164
I went to the underpass that day.

17:20.831 --> 17:23.500
I went over there
as soon as your grandfather called me,

17:23.584 --> 17:24.710
but I got there late.

17:24.793 --> 17:28.839
Then I saw those goons
lying on the ground and thought,

17:28.922 --> 17:30.090
"These guys can fight."

17:30.174 --> 17:31.050
[both chuckle]

17:32.051 --> 17:35.679
Remember when you wanted
to be a boxing champion back then?

17:35.763 --> 17:38.766
- That was a long time ago.
- What is it?

17:40.517 --> 17:41.351
We got a hit.

17:42.895 --> 17:43.937
Who?

17:44.021 --> 17:45.355
The sales director.

17:45.439 --> 17:47.066
Let's talk in the back.

17:47.149 --> 17:49.443
What? Why? They're coming with us.

17:49.985 --> 17:51.487
[Du-yeong] What are you talking about?

17:51.987 --> 17:54.740
- What's the problem?
- It'll make them all accomplices.

17:56.617 --> 17:58.702
Hey, they're the ones who wanted in.

17:58.786 --> 17:59.787
[sighs]

18:01.830 --> 18:06.168
Listen, once you have a record,
boxing days are over. Got it?

18:06.794 --> 18:08.003
Yeah.

18:10.672 --> 18:13.008
Why are you fighting Kim Myeong-gil,
Mr. Hwang?

18:13.092 --> 18:15.344
I'm here to finally avenge our boys.

18:15.427 --> 18:16.970
But you could die fighting him.

18:17.054 --> 18:18.764
Aren't you… afraid?

18:19.848 --> 18:23.060
What I'm really afraid of
is not managing to kill the fucker.

18:24.019 --> 18:24.853
[Du-yeong sighs]

18:25.437 --> 18:26.730
Okay, and what about you two?

18:26.814 --> 18:28.690
- I'm in.
- Me too.

18:28.774 --> 18:29.817
Why?

18:30.651 --> 18:32.569
Because Kim Myeong-gil is a bad man.

18:33.570 --> 18:36.657
My family would have been ruined
without the help of Mr. Choi.

18:37.491 --> 18:38.909
I'm only good at fighting,

18:40.244 --> 18:42.079
so I'll help however I can.

18:42.955 --> 18:43.872
Same here.

18:43.956 --> 18:46.458
These two Marines,
they're ready for your assistance, sir.

18:46.542 --> 18:47.918
You two are Marines?

18:48.001 --> 18:48.836
Yes.

18:49.378 --> 18:50.379
Are you a Marine?

18:50.963 --> 18:51.922
Exempted, but he was.

18:52.923 --> 18:54.758
Oh! [shallow breathing]

18:55.509 --> 18:56.760
Salute!

18:56.844 --> 18:58.262
[Du-yeong laughs]

19:01.265 --> 19:04.560
Hey, can you stop telling everyone
my personal shit, man?

19:04.643 --> 19:06.770
This is how you get to know people.

19:09.731 --> 19:11.316
Put your hands down.

19:11.400 --> 19:12.526
What was your class?

19:13.610 --> 19:14.778
Sit down.

19:16.029 --> 19:17.614
You are my senior Marine!

19:18.782 --> 19:20.284
Are you really going to make me get up?

19:20.868 --> 19:22.119
- Now sit down.
- [groans]

19:24.037 --> 19:26.331
Once a Marine, always a Marine, sir!

19:26.415 --> 19:28.792
- Whoa!
- Go easy on him.

19:29.293 --> 19:32.171
- This punk trying to one up on me.
- [groaning]

19:32.671 --> 19:35.090
[straining] No, sir.
It's the Marine spirit.

19:35.174 --> 19:36.592
Uh, sir, he's just high on pride.

19:36.675 --> 19:39.970
If you could let him off the hook
this one time.

19:40.554 --> 19:41.471
"High on pride"?

19:42.055 --> 19:43.974
Oh, uh, too much MCP, sir.

19:44.057 --> 19:45.184
And what is that, huh?

19:45.267 --> 19:47.811
- It's short for Marine Corps Pride.
- Ah.

19:47.895 --> 19:49.354
What's your class?

19:49.938 --> 19:51.565
He's high on MCP.

19:51.648 --> 19:53.025
Please tell me.

19:54.443 --> 19:55.360
[Woo-jin groans]

19:55.444 --> 19:58.238
571. Happy?

20:00.282 --> 20:01.158
Sir.

20:01.658 --> 20:03.118
Salute!

20:04.578 --> 20:05.412
[exhales deeply]

20:09.458 --> 20:10.584
And you?

20:11.585 --> 20:13.337
You think I can't put up a fight?

20:14.838 --> 20:16.423
Mr. Choi might worry about you.

20:17.382 --> 20:18.217
That's all.

20:19.593 --> 20:20.886
I started this thing.

20:21.553 --> 20:22.596
I'm gonna end it.

20:23.597 --> 20:24.431
[Du-yeong] Okay.

20:25.432 --> 20:26.308
[inhales sharply]

20:26.934 --> 20:27.768
Okay.

20:28.936 --> 20:30.103
We strike tonight.

20:30.938 --> 20:34.608
Once you take down the sales director,
you'll have to call me directly.

20:34.691 --> 20:36.109
I'll be at the hospital.

20:36.193 --> 20:37.444
Got it.

20:37.527 --> 20:39.238
Why do we have to wait to go in?

20:39.321 --> 20:42.616
If the director has goons protecting him,
they're onto us.

20:42.699 --> 20:44.201
That means thugs are at the hospital.

20:45.285 --> 20:47.162
Isn't it dangerous
for Du-yeong to go in alone?

20:48.330 --> 20:49.498
He's too fast for them.

20:49.581 --> 20:51.583
[uptempo electronic music playing]

20:51.667 --> 20:54.544
Wouldn't it be safer
if we all ganged up on Kim Jun-min,

20:54.628 --> 20:55.963
and went with him to the hospital?

20:56.672 --> 21:00.759
Once they know that we're coming for them,
it's going to be all hands on deck.

21:01.468 --> 21:02.511
And we're dead.

21:03.095 --> 21:04.179
There's too many.

21:04.888 --> 21:07.599
That's why we split up
and hit at the same time.

21:07.683 --> 21:11.645
- [Du-yeong] Mm-hm.
- It's risky, but it's how we win this.

21:12.229 --> 21:13.146
[Du-yeong inhales]

21:14.982 --> 21:16.275
I'm on a motorcycle.

21:17.276 --> 21:19.069
I'll dip if it gets rough.

21:21.822 --> 21:23.115
What do you think we should do?

21:24.449 --> 21:25.701
Can you ride a motorcycle?

21:26.618 --> 21:27.703
No.

21:27.786 --> 21:29.288
They're way too fast.

21:29.871 --> 21:30.706
What?

21:31.581 --> 21:32.749
Nothing, sir.

21:33.959 --> 21:35.669
I'll bring these guys with me.

21:35.752 --> 21:37.004
I may need help at the hospital.

21:37.087 --> 21:37.921
Okay.

21:38.005 --> 21:39.631
Then I'll go with Du-yeong, okay?

21:39.715 --> 21:40.882
I'll bring my bike.

21:42.009 --> 21:42.843
All right.

21:43.510 --> 21:44.511
Shall we have some food?

21:45.095 --> 21:46.346
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

21:46.430 --> 21:47.973
I didn't know you rode.

21:48.557 --> 21:49.725
- Yeah.
- What kind?

21:50.225 --> 21:51.518
I ride a naked bike.

21:52.477 --> 21:54.354
Hey, we look kinda similar, yeah?

21:55.605 --> 21:56.732
- Right?
- [Yang-jung] Yeah.

21:57.607 --> 21:58.483
Damn it. [groans]

21:58.567 --> 22:00.235
[Du-yeong] Why are you mad? We look good.

22:00.319 --> 22:01.445
Where'd you serve, sir?

22:01.528 --> 22:03.155
Just leave it be.

22:03.739 --> 22:05.032
Stop it, man.

22:05.741 --> 22:06.783
Hey, Min-dong.

22:07.326 --> 22:10.370
- Get some soup and rice.
- Yes, sir.

22:12.331 --> 22:13.165
[Du-yeong] Duk.

22:13.665 --> 22:15.625
- How are you?
- Oh, good. Been a while.

22:16.293 --> 22:17.210
This is my friend.

22:17.294 --> 22:18.545
- Oh, hello.
- Hi.

22:19.379 --> 22:20.464
I've already prepped.

22:21.965 --> 22:24.509
[sighs] The new ones are beautiful.

22:24.593 --> 22:26.303
[uptempo electronic music playing]

22:26.887 --> 22:30.515
- Have you ridden one?
- Yeah, briefly a while back.

22:31.475 --> 22:32.851
You're both Marines.

22:32.934 --> 22:35.062
They taught you how to use knives, right?

22:35.145 --> 22:36.855
- Try this.
- Oh, no.

22:37.898 --> 22:38.732
They didn't?

22:38.815 --> 22:39.900
- No.
- No.

22:43.904 --> 22:44.946
Then take these.

22:45.030 --> 22:48.575
Sir, are we… planning on using knives?

22:50.243 --> 22:53.413
- Did I just say that?
- Well, you just offered them.

22:53.997 --> 22:55.207
I did.

22:55.290 --> 22:56.500
I'm sorry, sir!

22:59.044 --> 23:02.881
You need to know how to use a knife,
so you can counter someone using one.

23:03.465 --> 23:04.925
You need to know how they think.

23:05.008 --> 23:06.718
- Oh.
- [shouts]

23:06.802 --> 23:07.636
You scared me.

23:10.097 --> 23:12.808
Okay. This one's yours.

23:14.226 --> 23:15.102
It's the fastest.

23:16.937 --> 23:18.146
[engine starts]

23:18.688 --> 23:21.983
[engine revving]

23:23.360 --> 23:24.319
It suits you.

23:25.695 --> 23:29.950
Sashimi knives don't have a guard
between the hilt and blade.

23:30.033 --> 23:31.827
Because it's not meant to stab.

23:32.744 --> 23:34.871
Now, look. If you stab hard,

23:36.498 --> 23:39.501
your hand slides forward,
and the blade fucks you up.

23:39.584 --> 23:41.002
If you want to stab with this,

23:41.086 --> 23:42.796
you need to support the end.

23:43.463 --> 23:45.674
- And that…
- [exhales]

23:45.757 --> 23:47.092
…prevents slipping.

23:47.843 --> 23:50.804
[exhales] If they come at you like this,
what do you think they're going for?

23:50.887 --> 23:53.390
They're probably trying to slash
your hand or wrist, sir.

23:53.473 --> 23:55.600
That's right. Not a kill attack.

23:56.685 --> 24:00.021
In boxing terms,
it would be like throwing light jabs.

24:00.105 --> 24:01.398
- Mm-hm.
- Ah.

24:03.316 --> 24:06.695
- [grunts]
- Once more! Keep it up.

24:07.988 --> 24:09.906
Loosen up and keep circling.

24:12.784 --> 24:13.743
[grunts]

24:15.203 --> 24:16.079
[laughs]

24:18.457 --> 24:20.834
And if they're supporting the hilt
with both hands,

24:20.917 --> 24:23.170
It's the kill. [hisses]

24:25.589 --> 24:27.674
If you push down the knife
with your thumb,

24:27.757 --> 24:30.343
your hand won't slide
unless there's a lot of force behind it.

24:31.136 --> 24:34.139
If they're using this grip,
it means they're experienced.

24:34.222 --> 24:36.516
You're swinging like a bat.

24:36.600 --> 24:37.851
- So relax?
- It's too much force.

24:37.934 --> 24:38.894
- Uh-huh.
- That's right.

24:47.110 --> 24:48.153
That's it!

24:54.409 --> 24:55.494
[both laughing]

24:56.203 --> 24:57.287
[tires screeching]

24:58.914 --> 25:01.583
- [goon 1] What the hell? Amazing.
- [goon 2] Show me. Show me.

25:01.666 --> 25:03.502
[goon 1] Try to fuck with me,
and I'll kill you.

25:03.585 --> 25:04.753
[ominous music playing]

25:04.836 --> 25:06.087
[goon 3] Deal the cards.

25:06.171 --> 25:08.340
- [goon 1] Fuck. Let me have this.
- [goon 2] Hey, show me.

25:10.759 --> 25:11.927
What's up, man?

25:15.472 --> 25:16.556
- [grunts]
- [groans]

25:16.640 --> 25:19.184
- [grunts]
- [choking]

25:19.267 --> 25:20.810
You fucking pricks!

25:23.980 --> 25:26.024
[In-beom panting]

25:30.111 --> 25:31.488
[suspenseful music playing]

25:39.371 --> 25:41.039
We'll wait here. [exhales deeply]

25:54.261 --> 25:56.263
[tense music playing]

26:05.564 --> 26:06.690
[guard] Whoa, whoa!

26:07.732 --> 26:09.734
- Which apartment are you visiting?
- [goon] 603.

26:12.737 --> 26:14.072
A car is coming.

26:16.449 --> 26:17.409
[inhales sharply]

26:31.214 --> 26:32.257
There's a goon.

26:32.882 --> 26:33.717
What now?

26:35.051 --> 26:36.469
- We'll wait.
- [cell phone vibrating]

26:41.266 --> 26:42.851
INCOMING CALL

26:42.934 --> 26:44.060
Damn it.

26:45.103 --> 26:46.146
[exhales deeply]

26:51.401 --> 26:53.111
[shaky breathing]

26:59.075 --> 26:59.909
[music ends]

27:06.207 --> 27:07.042
Thank you.

27:08.043 --> 27:09.044
Now, listen.

27:09.127 --> 27:11.129
If you want to survive doing this work,

27:11.212 --> 27:12.797
you gotta sell everything.

27:14.090 --> 27:14.924
All of it.

27:15.592 --> 27:17.552
Your fists, soul,

27:18.595 --> 27:19.888
all of your dreams.

27:21.181 --> 27:23.850
But you can never sell out
your friends and family.

27:24.434 --> 27:25.852
That's no way for you to live.

27:27.437 --> 27:28.688
- Yeah.
- Yes.

27:29.898 --> 27:31.733
Once we're inside the hospital,

27:31.816 --> 27:34.152
if I tell you guys to run,
don't argue and just run.

27:34.235 --> 27:36.071
I'll take care of things myself.

27:37.864 --> 27:38.740
[exhales deeply]

27:38.823 --> 27:40.075
You hear me?

27:41.159 --> 27:45.205
You just said not to abandon our friends
or family, right, sir?

27:45.789 --> 27:46.956
I'm a criminal.

27:47.040 --> 27:50.418
We may be in the same boat right now,
but we're not a family, all right?

27:51.211 --> 27:52.420
We'll never meet again.

27:52.921 --> 27:55.423
So don't get attached
to any of this, okay?

28:01.554 --> 28:02.639
Understood?

28:03.556 --> 28:04.391
Yeah.

28:06.685 --> 28:07.519
Yeah.

28:11.231 --> 28:12.273
[exhales deeply]

28:19.823 --> 28:21.199
[tense music playing]

28:26.579 --> 28:27.664
Kim Jun-min is here.

28:30.458 --> 28:31.876
[breathes deeply]

28:33.461 --> 28:34.796
[Hyeon-ju] What should we do?

28:36.506 --> 28:38.049
Mr. Lee, what do we do?

28:39.342 --> 28:40.301
Can you hear me?

28:40.927 --> 28:43.221
- Just answer me.
- It's a go.

28:43.304 --> 28:44.305
[exhales sharply]

28:44.389 --> 28:45.390
[music intensifies]

28:49.310 --> 28:50.270
[car approaching]

28:50.353 --> 28:52.355
[tires screeching]

28:55.567 --> 28:56.568
[horn honking]

28:58.194 --> 28:59.529
[engine revving]

29:00.405 --> 29:02.282
Ah, shit. This asshole!

29:05.410 --> 29:07.537
[choking]

29:09.622 --> 29:11.416
[choking, grunts]

29:11.499 --> 29:13.168
- [strained breathing]
- [door closes]

29:13.251 --> 29:15.754
- [goon 1] Fuck!
- [goon 2] Call the hospital, idiot!

29:15.837 --> 29:17.797
[choking]

29:23.052 --> 29:24.053
[tires screeching]

29:24.137 --> 29:25.388
[engine revving]

29:25.472 --> 29:26.514
[Du-yeong groans]

29:31.895 --> 29:33.813
- [Du-yeong groaning]
- [goon 3] You son of a bitch!

29:34.856 --> 29:35.815
[Du-yeong groaning]

29:35.899 --> 29:37.317
[goon 3 grunting]

29:37.984 --> 29:40.236
- You motherfucker!
- Die, asshole.

29:40.862 --> 29:43.239
[groaning]

29:43.823 --> 29:44.908
[goon 2 grunts]

29:45.950 --> 29:48.870
- Do-hu, put this asshole in the trunk.
- [Du-yeong groaning]

29:48.953 --> 29:50.330
- [engine revs]
- Get him up!

29:51.206 --> 29:53.208
- [engine revving]
- [rock music playing]

29:54.459 --> 29:55.293
What the hell?

29:56.002 --> 29:56.836
[yelps]

29:57.420 --> 29:59.214
Who is that fucker?!

30:02.467 --> 30:04.219
- [Du-yeong grunts]
- [groans]

30:05.220 --> 30:06.054
Fuck!

30:07.847 --> 30:10.016
Hey! Whoa, whoa! [yelps]

30:10.517 --> 30:11.726
- [grunts]
- [groans]

30:12.811 --> 30:14.979
[panting]

30:21.986 --> 30:22.821
Are you okay?

30:24.489 --> 30:25.698
[exhales deeply]

30:41.047 --> 30:42.632
MAIN BUILDING
PATIENT ROOM, BLOCK 17

30:42.715 --> 30:44.843
DU-YEONG

30:46.761 --> 30:47.637
What's up?

30:50.098 --> 30:50.974
You all right?

30:52.183 --> 30:53.017
Okay.

31:02.861 --> 31:04.070
Let's go.

31:04.153 --> 31:05.280
- Okay.
- Yes, sir.

31:12.161 --> 31:13.746
[suspenseful music playing]

31:35.435 --> 31:36.519
[tense music playing]

31:40.398 --> 31:41.232
That was Im Jang-do.

31:41.316 --> 31:42.859
[music intensifies]

31:46.863 --> 31:48.573
BITCOIN

31:48.656 --> 31:50.408
That's right, up you go.

31:53.786 --> 31:54.621
Damn it!

32:06.090 --> 32:09.052
[all shouting, cheering]

32:10.511 --> 32:11.346
[grunts]

32:16.225 --> 32:18.311
[all panting]

32:18.394 --> 32:20.438
[patients shouting]

32:20.521 --> 32:22.065
- [Yang-jung grunts]
- [Jang-do groans]

32:23.274 --> 32:24.275
I know. We're just--

32:25.944 --> 32:26.861
Hold on.

32:27.528 --> 32:28.655
[Jang-do grunts] Damn it!

32:30.615 --> 32:31.741
[Jang-do grunting]

32:36.704 --> 32:37.997
- [goon] The hell?
- [Woo-jin gasps]

32:38.081 --> 32:38.957
[Yang-jung groans]

32:39.040 --> 32:39.958
[groans]

32:40.041 --> 32:42.377
- [Woo-jin grunting]
- [groans]

32:45.880 --> 32:46.714
[yells]

32:52.178 --> 32:53.513
[Jang-do grunts]

32:56.808 --> 32:58.017
[Jang-do groaning]

33:05.525 --> 33:06.693
[music ends]

33:06.776 --> 33:07.944
[all panting]

33:08.027 --> 33:09.737
- Let's go.
- [Gun-woo] Okay.

33:09.821 --> 33:11.197
[suspenseful music playing]

33:15.326 --> 33:16.953
- Careful.
- [Woo-jin] Okay.

33:30.091 --> 33:31.217
[cell phone vibrating]

33:34.303 --> 33:35.304
[sighs]

33:38.307 --> 33:41.394
WE'VE GOT IM JANG-DO
TAKING HIM TO DU-YEONG'S STORE

33:43.354 --> 33:44.272
[exhales]

33:59.787 --> 34:00.621
[Du-yeong] Gentlemen.

34:00.705 --> 34:01.956
- [Woo-jin] Hello.
- [Gun-woo] Hello.

34:09.839 --> 34:10.840
Put him in that.

34:10.923 --> 34:11.966
[Woo-jin hesitating] Yes.

34:14.052 --> 34:15.261
- One, two… [grunts]
- [grunts]

34:15.344 --> 34:16.763
[Du-yeong] Careful with him.

34:16.846 --> 34:18.765
[both grunting]

34:19.265 --> 34:20.600
[Yang-jung] Where's the salt?

34:20.683 --> 34:21.517
Salt?

34:23.144 --> 34:24.062
In the office.

34:25.104 --> 34:26.397
Go make some salt water.

34:27.148 --> 34:29.567
- [groans]
- Find a bucket, dump it in.

34:29.650 --> 34:30.777
Okay.

34:30.860 --> 34:31.944
- Let's go.
- All right.

34:32.028 --> 34:32.862
In the corner.

34:32.945 --> 34:33.988
- [Gun-woo] Okay.
- [Woo-jin] Yes.

34:35.490 --> 34:36.532
[Du-yeong exhales deeply]

34:43.498 --> 34:44.957
[Gun-woo] Hyeon-ju, you okay?

34:45.041 --> 34:46.918
Yeah, are you all right?

34:47.001 --> 34:47.960
Mm-hm.

34:49.670 --> 34:51.672
We got Im Jang-do.

34:52.173 --> 34:53.466
- Mm-hm.
- What about you?

34:53.549 --> 34:56.344
Uh, I was outside, but Du-yeong got him.

34:56.427 --> 34:59.472
- Oh.
- He killed him?

35:03.976 --> 35:04.894
[exhales deeply]

35:05.853 --> 35:07.230
Let's go make the salt water.

35:07.313 --> 35:08.731
- Come on.
- Uh-huh.

35:12.860 --> 35:14.570
- [metal clanking]
- [Gun-woo] We can use this.

35:14.654 --> 35:16.072
- Water?
- I think I saw it downstairs.

35:16.155 --> 35:16.989
Let's go.

35:17.073 --> 35:18.157
Hyeon-ju, come on.

35:26.040 --> 35:27.333
[cell phone vibrating]

35:32.839 --> 35:33.756
Yeah?

35:33.840 --> 35:36.676
I'll be there in five minutes,
so shake him up a little.

35:36.759 --> 35:41.264
Oh, and… have Hyeon-ju and the guys watch.

35:42.890 --> 35:44.767
[light instrumental music playing]

35:51.440 --> 35:52.483
[sighs]

35:55.611 --> 35:56.779
What's up?

35:56.863 --> 35:57.780
[sighs]

35:58.281 --> 35:59.824
He told me to have Hyeon-ju watch.

35:59.907 --> 36:00.867
Why?

36:03.744 --> 36:05.121
I hope she can take it.

36:07.415 --> 36:09.167
Hello, sir. This way.

36:09.250 --> 36:10.585
[ominous music playing]

36:23.973 --> 36:26.184
Stop. Now show us the stairs.

36:26.267 --> 36:27.894
We don't have cameras on that side.

36:28.519 --> 36:29.353
Why not?

36:29.437 --> 36:30.771
[guard] We just don't.

36:32.190 --> 36:33.024
[scoffs]

36:33.107 --> 36:34.817
Are you kidding me? You shit--

36:35.776 --> 36:37.737
So, tell me something.

36:38.404 --> 36:40.781
Are there any cameras facing the building?

36:40.865 --> 36:42.783
The police would probably have some.

36:51.542 --> 36:52.376
How's Jun-min?

36:54.378 --> 36:55.588
He's still unconscious.

36:56.756 --> 36:58.132
Go to the management office

36:58.216 --> 37:00.635
and get the plates
of the fuckers who attacked him.

37:00.718 --> 37:01.552
Yes.

37:03.095 --> 37:04.722
- [grunting]
- Right there, man.

37:04.805 --> 37:05.973
How much do we pour in?

37:06.557 --> 37:08.434
Uh, didn't he tell us to use it all?

37:09.227 --> 37:10.228
It's a lot.

37:10.311 --> 37:13.481
[sighs] Let's put it all in.
I guess that's what he wants.

37:14.398 --> 37:15.441
Okay.

37:18.736 --> 37:19.612
But why?

37:19.695 --> 37:20.696
Making salt water.

37:26.953 --> 37:27.870
Bring it here.

37:27.954 --> 37:29.080
Uh, yes.

37:33.209 --> 37:34.418
Sit down and watch.

37:36.170 --> 37:37.004
Why?

37:37.088 --> 37:38.673
Mr. Choi's orders.

37:40.549 --> 37:41.634
[Yang-jung blows air]

37:43.928 --> 37:44.929
[blows air]

37:46.472 --> 37:50.059
My pet peeve is people not talking
when they say they're going to.

37:51.310 --> 37:55.731
That means you'll nod your head
only when you have something to say to us.

37:55.815 --> 37:56.649
[blows air]

37:57.275 --> 38:01.028
Because if you nod and don't talk,
I promise I will cut your lips off.

38:01.112 --> 38:01.988
Got it?

38:06.867 --> 38:07.702
[grunts]

38:13.374 --> 38:14.917
[muffled screaming]

38:15.001 --> 38:16.460
[tense music playing]

38:20.172 --> 38:21.007
[grunting]

38:29.765 --> 38:31.267
[muffled screaming]

38:33.644 --> 38:35.771
- [Jang-do groaning]
- [Woo-jin exhales]

38:37.898 --> 38:40.568
[panting]

38:40.651 --> 38:42.236
You don't want to talk?

38:42.737 --> 38:43.904
[breathing heavily]

38:46.073 --> 38:47.366
[sander whirring]

38:49.368 --> 38:50.703
[muffled screaming]

38:55.374 --> 38:57.209
[muffled screaming]

39:01.088 --> 39:02.381
[Jang-do groaning]

39:04.425 --> 39:05.551
[Jang-do whimpering]

39:07.386 --> 39:10.097
[muffled screaming]

39:14.560 --> 39:16.687
[Jang-do groaning]

39:16.771 --> 39:18.773
[muffled screaming]

39:19.357 --> 39:20.691
[breathing heavily]

39:23.652 --> 39:25.154
[muffled screaming]

39:25.237 --> 39:26.072
[gasps]

39:27.531 --> 39:29.241
[Jang-do groaning]

39:33.496 --> 39:34.538
[coughing]

39:35.206 --> 39:36.999
[retches, coughs]

39:38.793 --> 39:39.668
[inhales sharply]

39:41.212 --> 39:43.964
[coughing]

39:45.257 --> 39:46.550
[breathing heavily]

39:49.595 --> 39:51.430
- [Gun-woo] Hyeon-ju.
- [coughing]

39:53.557 --> 39:56.060
[Hyeon-ju coughing, spits]

40:05.152 --> 40:06.695
Why did you make me watch?

40:07.488 --> 40:10.616
Myeong-gil has probably started looking
for Im Jang-do by now.

40:11.367 --> 40:12.827
We don't have much time.

40:13.994 --> 40:16.288
You watched because I wanted you guys
to know something.

40:16.997 --> 40:18.499
[Hyeon-ju] What are you talking about?

40:19.083 --> 40:21.252
This is not going to end
until someone dies.

40:21.335 --> 40:23.754
And there's no guarantee
that someone won't be me.

40:24.422 --> 40:27.174
Why would you say something so horrible?

40:27.258 --> 40:28.926
- Hyeon-ju.
- That's enough.

40:29.427 --> 40:30.261
[exhales sharply]

40:30.344 --> 40:31.720
[soft piano music playing]

40:35.141 --> 40:36.142
[Mr. Choi] Hyeon-ju!

40:39.478 --> 40:41.105
Mr. Oh, look after her.

40:41.188 --> 40:42.064
Yes, sir.

40:43.399 --> 40:45.151
[Mr. Choi] Oh, goddammit, that kid.

40:49.155 --> 40:50.906
- Gun-woo.
- Uh, yes.

40:52.825 --> 40:53.701
If you end up…

40:55.786 --> 40:57.163
fighting Myeong-gil,

40:58.330 --> 40:59.748
can you protect the others?

41:01.250 --> 41:03.127
Will you please do that for me?

41:05.087 --> 41:06.505
With all of my will, sir.

41:08.007 --> 41:09.049
Thank you so much.

41:10.759 --> 41:12.136
We don't have much time.

41:12.803 --> 41:14.638
Let me teach you just one thing now.

41:14.722 --> 41:15.639
[exhales]

41:16.765 --> 41:17.600
[Mr. Choi sighs]

41:18.350 --> 41:22.480
In order to take down an organization,
all you need is

41:24.231 --> 41:26.650
dispersion and division.

41:28.444 --> 41:31.864
People tend to trust those
that know and empathize with them.

41:34.575 --> 41:36.785
If you're not able to gain their trust,

41:38.287 --> 41:40.331
your organization can be divided.

41:40.414 --> 41:42.291
- [sander whirring]
- [Jang-do groaning]

41:47.254 --> 41:51.300
- [muffled screaming]
- [sander turns off]

41:51.800 --> 41:54.220
[Jang-do grunting, panting]

41:55.387 --> 41:56.305
Take that off.

41:59.600 --> 42:00.434
[Jang-do grunts]

42:02.770 --> 42:03.896
[Jang-do panting]

42:05.022 --> 42:06.106
[grunts]

42:06.190 --> 42:07.983
[Jang-do panting]

42:12.947 --> 42:14.073
[Mr. Choi] Im Jang-do?

42:15.115 --> 42:16.909
I've been led to believe that you

42:17.785 --> 42:20.788
may be the one who understands Myeong-gil
the best of all his men.

42:21.997 --> 42:24.917
Myeong-gil is a very violent, cruel man.

42:25.584 --> 42:27.920
But he's capable
of reading people like a book.

42:28.754 --> 42:30.256
He truly gets them.

42:31.173 --> 42:34.510
I'm sure plenty of his men
take him at his word.

42:36.303 --> 42:37.304
But you're smarter.

42:37.846 --> 42:39.056
You know Myeong-gil.

42:40.641 --> 42:44.478
You know he doesn't ever empathize
with any one of his people.

42:45.312 --> 42:47.106
He's cold and calculating.

42:47.815 --> 42:52.236
Always thinking how best to move
his little pieces to his advantage.

42:52.319 --> 42:55.906
You knew all this,
and you still decided to work for him.

42:56.907 --> 42:57.908
Why?

42:58.659 --> 43:00.536
At first, you were just led by greed.

43:02.079 --> 43:02.997
In only one year,

43:03.080 --> 43:06.625
he paid you what a major corporate gig
would have paid in five.

43:06.709 --> 43:10.337
Graduating from the Police Academy
was supposed to give you authority,

43:10.421 --> 43:12.673
but you ended up getting yourself demoted.

43:12.756 --> 43:14.925
It was all about your pride.

43:17.344 --> 43:21.390
I suppose that pride was the real reason
you were fine working for him after all.

43:22.057 --> 43:25.185
You were confident
that you could keep your sense of agency.

43:25.769 --> 43:27.104
You'd never lose that.

43:28.147 --> 43:30.232
Not to a low-life thug.

43:30.816 --> 43:33.277
And if by chance
he found some reason to kill you,

43:34.278 --> 43:36.947
you could just run off

43:38.115 --> 43:40.117
with the money you made working for him.

43:43.954 --> 43:45.414
Hm, I like that plan.

43:46.457 --> 43:50.586
If I took your photo
and decided to sent it to him right now

43:51.670 --> 43:54.923
and said that you gave me the names
of the people he had you kill,

43:55.007 --> 43:57.259
he would surely believe me over you.

43:57.343 --> 44:01.263
After all, what man wouldn't squeal
if they were in your current position?

44:04.183 --> 44:07.436
Then he'd call back
all the men he sent out to find you…

44:07.519 --> 44:08.395
[shaky breathing]

44:08.479 --> 44:10.689
…unleash a pack of bloodhounds,

44:10.773 --> 44:12.733
and they'll kill you in no time.

44:13.734 --> 44:16.612
You wouldn't even get a chance
to plead your case.

44:17.780 --> 44:18.989
He won't let you.

44:19.073 --> 44:21.408
Myeong-gil doesn't care about the truth.

44:22.076 --> 44:24.536
The math tells him to bury you.

44:26.205 --> 44:28.040
I mean,
if there is one person on the planet

44:28.123 --> 44:31.168
who knows every single one
of Myeong-gil's crimes,

44:31.251 --> 44:33.087
that person is you, isn't it?

44:36.757 --> 44:38.967
You know him just as well as I do.

44:40.344 --> 44:45.057
If I plant even the smallest seed
of doubt about you to Myeong-gil…

44:47.851 --> 44:49.353
you are a dead man.

44:49.978 --> 44:50.854
Fuck.

44:52.022 --> 44:53.732
Wait. Damn it.

44:55.150 --> 44:57.319
Why should I die?!

44:58.112 --> 44:59.446
Fuck me!

44:59.530 --> 45:00.406
Im Jang-do!

45:00.489 --> 45:01.949
[screams, groans]

45:02.032 --> 45:03.826
Shut up and listen to me!

45:03.909 --> 45:06.537
If you don't pull yourself together,
you will die.

45:06.620 --> 45:08.622
[shallow breathing]

45:11.583 --> 45:12.793
Tell me everything.

45:14.586 --> 45:17.506
And I will send you to a safe country
far away from here

45:17.589 --> 45:19.550
with more than enough money to live.

45:20.551 --> 45:22.219
I taught Myeong-gil everything.

45:23.804 --> 45:26.432
I know of places
that he hasn't even heard of.

45:27.057 --> 45:28.142
This is a promise.

45:30.769 --> 45:31.937
[shaky breathing]

45:32.020 --> 45:35.107
You were already planning to leave
sooner or later.

45:36.400 --> 45:38.527
I'm giving you the chance to do it.

45:38.610 --> 45:40.446
[shaky breathing]

45:44.032 --> 45:45.033
If I talk,

45:46.535 --> 45:47.828
how much money?

45:49.830 --> 45:50.914
[choking]

45:50.998 --> 45:52.750
I'd answer quickly if I were you.,

45:53.459 --> 45:55.085
[Jang-do heavy, rapid breathing]

45:57.129 --> 45:58.213
[coughs]

45:59.965 --> 46:03.135
Myeong-gil and Smile Capital
are going down for good.

46:03.218 --> 46:05.721
- [scoffs]
- After that, you're in Guam.

46:05.804 --> 46:07.389
I know some people there.

46:08.182 --> 46:11.810
You'll have plenty enough
to start a new life.

46:20.444 --> 46:21.528
Get him some clothes.

46:37.169 --> 46:38.378
How long have you worked for him?

46:39.463 --> 46:40.506
Five years.

46:40.589 --> 46:42.341
And what is it you do exactly?

46:42.925 --> 46:46.595
I ensure Mr. Kim's illegal dealings
fly under police radar

46:46.678 --> 46:50.182
and make sure things run smoothly
if the police do sniff around.

46:50.265 --> 46:52.309
All right, but what did you do?

46:52.392 --> 46:54.770
For small stuff,
me and In-beom handled it.

46:54.853 --> 46:57.523
And for bigger things,
we used Kim's service company.

46:58.148 --> 46:59.399
What small stuff?

46:59.483 --> 47:01.485
Like… [groans]

47:02.027 --> 47:03.987
…filming things to use against people.

47:04.071 --> 47:06.406
- [Jang-do panting]
- You threatened Iil Group, am I right?

47:09.243 --> 47:10.244
Tell me.

47:11.411 --> 47:12.913
Look, Mr. Kim made me do it.

47:12.996 --> 47:15.707
He didn't ask you who made you do it.
He asked you what you did.

47:17.709 --> 47:19.711
I gathered some footage
of the Iil Group heir.

47:19.795 --> 47:20.921
And?

47:21.713 --> 47:25.342
[spluttering] We just… We stripped him.

47:25.425 --> 47:26.260
Why?

47:28.971 --> 47:31.056
Tell me everything from the start.

47:31.139 --> 47:32.057
[inhales sharply]

47:32.724 --> 47:35.686
There was a 40-story boutique hotel
being built in Gangnam,

47:35.769 --> 47:38.647
but the company went bankrupt
during the pandemic.

47:39.690 --> 47:40.941
Mr. Kim got wind of intel

47:41.024 --> 47:43.944
that the Iil Group heir
was going to take over the hotel project.

47:44.027 --> 47:45.279
But from whom?

47:46.113 --> 47:49.491
The hotel became an eyesore,
so Seoul City decided to step in.

47:49.575 --> 47:52.160
They were looking for someone with cash.

47:52.244 --> 47:55.914
An assemblyman who plays golf with Mr. Kim
recommended him to the mayor.

47:57.124 --> 48:01.169
He wants the… hotel to become a casino.

48:03.714 --> 48:06.300
Seoul City said they'd grant him
a permit for it.

48:07.009 --> 48:08.343
Mr. Kim got excited.

48:08.427 --> 48:10.554
But the Iil Group heir tried to back out,

48:11.221 --> 48:13.056
so I forced him to cooperate.

48:13.932 --> 48:16.184
How many people have you taken videos of?

48:16.935 --> 48:17.769
Fifty.

48:19.187 --> 48:21.481
And Myeong-gil still has all of them?

48:21.565 --> 48:22.399
Yeah.

48:23.358 --> 48:25.819
He sees people's weakness
as a source of income.

48:26.737 --> 48:30.908
He never gets rid of anything
that's of value to him.

48:31.575 --> 48:33.368
Where does he keep these videos?

48:33.452 --> 48:34.453
[inhales deeply]

48:35.287 --> 48:38.373
He keeps an encrypted hard drive
in a safe inside his bedroom.

48:38.999 --> 48:40.334
But it's this German smart safe.

48:41.752 --> 48:43.462
It has a biometric lock.

48:44.171 --> 48:47.090
And if he knows
there are any issues arising,

48:47.174 --> 48:49.343
he can incinerate everything inside it.

48:49.426 --> 48:51.845
He can press a button on his phone,

48:51.929 --> 48:53.805
and this thing will burn its contents.

48:53.889 --> 48:54.723
Nothing left.

48:54.806 --> 48:57.309
He knows
that this is a double-edged sword.

48:57.392 --> 49:01.229
A weapon in his hands
but evidence for the police.

49:02.856 --> 49:05.442
The service company, is it a gang?

49:05.984 --> 49:06.818
Yeah.

49:07.361 --> 49:08.195
How big?

49:08.779 --> 49:12.157
I believe it's around 30,
but they can get more.

49:12.240 --> 49:13.325
And who runs it?

49:13.951 --> 49:14.993
It's Mr. Jung.

49:15.494 --> 49:17.579
He's basically Mr. Kim's guard dog.

49:17.663 --> 49:19.539
He was an MMA fighter,

49:19.623 --> 49:22.709
but apparently he was banned
for beating a man to death in the octagon.

49:23.293 --> 49:24.670
That's when he was recruited.

49:24.753 --> 49:26.380
Who handles the bodies?

49:27.130 --> 49:28.966
Mr. Jung takes care of that.

49:29.466 --> 49:31.134
Tell me everything you know.

49:32.594 --> 49:33.679
Three years ago,

49:34.429 --> 49:38.183
Mr. Kim had a bit too much to drink
and killed a man with his bare hands.

49:38.266 --> 49:39.476
[sighs]

49:39.559 --> 49:40.894
I was nearby at the time,

49:40.978 --> 49:43.730
so I handled the scene
until Mr. Jung arrived.

49:43.814 --> 49:46.316
He called a 3-ton fish truck
with an aquarium

49:46.400 --> 49:47.818
and carried the body away.

49:48.777 --> 49:52.155
From the way he spoke to the driver,
it seemed like he did this a lot.

49:52.948 --> 49:53.907
The name?

49:55.826 --> 49:57.160
I don't remember the name.

49:58.954 --> 49:59.955
I see.

50:00.664 --> 50:02.374
I know a hospital in Incheon.

50:02.916 --> 50:05.252
I'll call an ambulance,
and you'll get some rest.

50:05.335 --> 50:06.920
Once everything is over,

50:07.421 --> 50:10.841
I'll arrange a flight and ID for you.

50:15.137 --> 50:16.972
Do not try to contact anyone.

50:18.056 --> 50:19.391
Otherwise, he'll find you.

50:19.975 --> 50:20.809
[exhales]

50:24.771 --> 50:26.690
[Du-yeong] Your phone. I'm keeping it.

50:29.484 --> 50:30.360
[Mr. Choi grunts]

50:34.156 --> 50:35.782
Let me ask you one last thing.

50:38.201 --> 50:40.287
Where does he keep his gold stashed?

50:41.705 --> 50:43.248
Only In-beom knows.

50:44.833 --> 50:45.834
Tell me why that is.

50:45.917 --> 50:48.920
In-beom is the only person Mr. Kim trusts.

50:49.546 --> 50:50.630
They met in prison.

50:50.714 --> 50:53.425
and they've saved each other's lives
multiple times.

50:53.508 --> 50:55.802
In-beom would give his life for him.

50:56.845 --> 50:59.014
I don't know everything
Mr. Kim is thinking,

50:59.514 --> 51:01.933
but I know In-beom is like a brother.

51:03.518 --> 51:05.312
[ominous music playing]

51:19.659 --> 51:21.078
[theme music playing]

53:09.603 --> 53:10.562
[theme music ends]
